// South of Mala Tokmachka, 8 June 2023: the 47th Brigade's breach into the Russian minefields.
// The history is in db/research/chapters/c09-robotyne.md (§3, §5, §6 set piece 1). The box is the same size as
// Vuhledar's. +x is east, +z south: the attack climbs from the N08 highway in the north (about 70 m) to the crest
// in the south (about 110 m), and the fields between are a grid of tree lines. The schema is bav_core::data.
(
    place: ("Mala Tokmachka", "Мала Токмачка"),
    date: "8 June 2023",
    tally_date: "08 JUN 2023",
    day_start_min: 230.0,
    compression: 0.30,
    attacker: Ua,
    summer: true,
    // Fictional, the 47th's own: the player (peregrine), the guns (thunder), the observers on the water tower (crane,
    // the old well sweep), the command post (cliff).
    callsigns: (player: ("Sapsan", "Сапсан"), guns: ("Hrim", "Грім"), op: ("Zhuravel", "Журавель"), command: ("Skelia", "Скеля")),
    anchor: (lat: 47.4967, lon: 35.8968, x: 0.0, z: 0.0, m_per_lon: 75250.0),

    // What the day says (design/hostomel.md, phase 0): the briefing, the lines that are this place's, the debrief's close.
    words: (
        briefing: r#"SOUTH OF MALA TOKMACHKA (МАЛА ТОКМАЧКА)
8 JUNE 2023

South of Orikhiv (Оріхів) the steppe climbs towards Tokmak (Токмак) through fields cut by tree lines.
Since the autumn Russia has dug in across it: minefields hundreds of metres deep, a trench on every crest,
guns registered on every track.

Before dawn the 47th Mechanised Brigade (47-ма ОМБр «Маґура») goes forward with its new armour: Leopards and Bradleys,
mine plows in front. The guns have finished their preparation. The column is late.

You are with the brigade: a drone operator and a fire controller. These are our vehicles, and our men.
The morning will run whether or not you do anything. What you do decides what it costs.

Mouse: right-drag to look, wheel to zoom.  WASD: fly the drone.  Q/E: turn.  R/F: climb/descend.
Left click: 155 mm fire mission (4 rounds).  Shift+click: smoke.  Ctrl+click: HIMARS.
Space: the column PUSH ON / HOLD / PULL BACK.  1/2 or Tab: drone / the water tower.  P: pause.  [ ]: time.
Alt+click: send a Bradley for the wounded there (four for the day).  V: answer the last call for evacuation.
4: fly the FPV (one today): mouse points it, W/S throttle, A/D bank.  M: move the drone team if they find you.
3: into the forward tree line with an ATGM team.  Right button: the sight.  Left click: launch.

Press Enter."#,
        op_label: "OBSERVER, WATER TOWER (СПОСТЕРІГАЧ, ВОДОНАПІРНА ВЕЖА)",
        op_lost: "The water tower is down. No eyes from the farm.",
        forward_belt: "the forward tree line",
        plow_mine: "Mine under the plow. Plow's gone. The rest of the lane is not cleared.",
        mine_lines: [
            "Mine! Left track gone. He's stuck in the lane.",
            "He went round the Leopard. Off the lane. Mine.",
            "Another one. They're everywhere off the plowed strip.",
            "Mine. Crew's alive, they're getting out.",
        ],
        registered: ("", "Incoming on the lane! They have it registered. Get out of there!"),
        closing: [
            "Within days the armour was stopped, and the brigades went forward on foot instead, a tree line at a time.",
            "Robotyne (Роботине), eleven kilometres to the south, was taken in August. Tokmak (Токмак) was not reached.",
        ],
        keys: "R: the same morning again, down the same tracks.     Esc: quit.",
        sources: [
            (publisher: "Popular Mechanics", date: "9 Jun 2023", title: "Ukraine's Western armor suffered enormous losses while breaching a minefield", url: "https://www.popularmechanics.com/military/weapons/a44157100/ukraine-suffers-losses-breaching-minefield/"),
            (publisher: "Euromaidan Press", date: "10 Jun 2023", title: "So how many Leopard tanks did Ukraine lose near Mala Tokmachka?", url: "https://euromaidanpress.com/2023/06/10/so-how-many-leopard-tanks-were-lost-in-ukraine/"),
            (publisher: "The Guardian", date: "14 Jun 2023", title: "Ukraine's failed Mala Tokmachka assault lays bare counteroffensive challenges", url: "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/14/ukraine-failed-assault-near-mala-tokmachka-raises-counteroffensive-challenges"),
            (publisher: "The War Zone", date: "15 Jun 2023", title: "Ukraine's armor appears to have a Russian attack helicopter problem", url: "https://www.twz.com/ukraines-armor-appears-to-have-a-russian-attack-helicopter-problem"),
            (publisher: "BBC News", date: "27 Jul 2023", title: "Western armour struggles against Russian defences", url: "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-66306150"),
            (publisher: "War on the Rocks", date: "4 Sep 2023", title: "Perseverance and adaptation: Ukraine's counteroffensive at three months", url: "https://warontherocks.com/2023/09/perseverance-and-adaptation-ukraines-counteroffensive-at-three-months/"),
            (publisher: "RUSI", date: "Sep 2023", title: "Stormbreak: fighting through Russian defences in Ukraine's 2023 offensive", url: "https://static.rusi.org/Stormbreak-Special-Report-web-final_0.pdf"),
            (publisher: "Kyiv Independent", date: "26 Sep 2023", title: "Overcoming setbacks, NATO-trained brigade breaches Surovikin line", url: "https://kyivindependent.com/overcoming-setbacks-nato-trained-brigade-breaches-surovikin-line-in-zaporizhzhia-oblast/"),
        ],
    ),
    // Where the drone starts, and what the observers fire from (their error grows with the distance from it).
    camera: (80.0, -1150.0),
    observed_from: Home,

    ground: [
        // The long open slope up from the Kinska valley to the crest: the attackers climb under observation, so the
        // slope is concave to the crest (no dead ground below it), and levels off behind the trench.
        Ramp(base: 68.0, amp: 42.0, power: 1.6, ramp: Rising(-2000.0, 700.0)),
        RidgeZ(z: 850.0, width: 320.0, amp: 4.0),
        // Long low swells, and a little roughness.
        Noise(scale: 1200.0, octaves: 3, seed: 17, amp: 4.5),
        Noise(scale: 240.0, octaves: 3, seed: 19, amp: 0.8),
        // A balka running north off the slope on the east side, and a shallower one in the west.
        Gully(x0: 1350.0, amp: 120.0, period: 500.0, z_offset: 0.0, phase: 0.0, width: 60.0, depth: 8.0, fade: Out(-500.0, 700.0)),
        Gully(x0: -1400.0, amp: 90.0, period: 380.0, z_offset: 0.0, phase: 1.0, width: 45.0, depth: 4.0, fade: Out(-900.0, -100.0)),
    ],

    curves: [
        // The N08 highway, Polohy–Voskresenka, running east-south-east across the north of the box.
        ("n08", (base: -1380.0, slope: 0.137)),
    ],

    lines: [
        ("n08", Sampled(curve: "n08", x0: -2364.0, span: 4728.0, n: 24)),
        // The two tracks south, each along the east side of a north-south tree line: "a wide muddy track between
        // hedgerows" (Guardian). Dry on 8 June: dust, not mud.
        ("west", Smoothed([(-470.0, -1795.0), (-492.0, -1450.0), (-503.0, -1000.0), (-498.0, -500.0), (-494.0, 0.0), (-489.0, 400.0), (-482.0, 700.0), (-470.0, 1000.0)], 3)),
        ("east", Smoothed([(704.0, -1795.0), (690.0, -1300.0), (676.0, -800.0), (667.0, -300.0), (661.0, 200.0), (656.0, 600.0), (651.0, 720.0), (640.0, 1000.0)], 3)),
        // Field tracks along the Ukrainian forward tree line and behind the Russian one.
        ("lateral", Points([(-2350.0, -914.0), (2350.0, -914.0)])),
        ("rear", Points([(-2350.0, 1000.0), (2350.0, 1000.0)])),
    ],

    roads: [
        (line: "n08", width: 9.0, kind: Asphalt),
        (line: "west", width: 6.0, kind: Dirt),
        (line: "east", width: 6.0, kind: Dirt),
        (line: "lateral", width: 3.5, kind: Track),
        (line: "rear", width: 3.5, kind: Track),
    ],

    // Shelterbelts: main belts about 0.55 km apart east-west, cross-belts about 1.15 km apart (dossier §3, the OSM
    // and Sentinel-2 sample box around Robotyne). The second row is the Ukrainian forward tree line; the fifth, on
    // the crest, is the Russian position: wider, thicker.
    belts: [
        Rows(rows: [(-1450.0, 13.0), (-900.0, 17.0), (-350.0, 13.0), (200.0, 17.0), (720.0, 22.0), (1270.0, 17.0)], amp: 7.0, period: 340.0, phase_step: 1.7, x0: -2264.0, span: 4528.0, n: 40),
        Lines(lines: [((-1650.0, -1700.0), (-1662.0, 1650.0)), ((-520.0, -1700.0), (-532.0, 1650.0)), ((640.0, -1700.0), (628.0, 1650.0)), ((1780.0, -1700.0), (1768.0, 1650.0))], width: 12.0),
    ],

    // The columns deploy only once through the barrier, at the trench: they never got that far.
    routes: [
        (line: "west", deploy: (-485.0, 600.0), objective: (-470.0, 702.0)),
        (line: "east", deploy: (655.0, 600.0), objective: (650.0, 702.0)),
    ],

    // The Surovikin line's first belt: a forward field of older and remotely laid mines, then the barrier proper,
    // about 480 m deep (RUSI: 120 m growing to about 500 m), anti-tank mines stacked two high, anti-personnel mines
    // among them, across the tracks as well as the fields.
    barriers: [
        (z0: -430.0, z1: -250.0, at_per: 260.0, stacked: 0.0, ap_per: 400.0),
        (z0: 110.0, z1: 590.0, at_per: 95.0, stacked: 0.45, ap_per: 70.0),
    ],

    ua_positions: [
        // ATGM teams in the forward tree line, at the heads of the two tracks (where the belts' gaps let them see up
        // the lanes) and between, watching the crest 1.6 km away.
        (-520.0, -896.0), (640.0, -895.0), (260.0, -897.0),
        // Riflemen covering the start line.
        (-180.0, -895.0), (-1350.0, -896.0),
    ],
    ru_positions: [
        // The 291st's first line: platoon positions along the crest trench, Kornet teams at the heads of the tracks,
        // looking straight down them through the belts' gaps.
        (-1500.0, 702.0), (-930.0, 700.0), (-468.0, 702.0), (180.0, 699.0),
        (666.0, 702.0), (1350.0, 701.0), (1900.0, 702.0),
    ],

    // The map table's (design/command.md). Ours runs to the start line in the forward tree line; the grey zone is
    // the slope and its minefields, theirs the crest from just before the trench.
    grey_zone: (-800.0, 600.0),
    // Where the 47th's columns come in: down the two tracks from the N08, and the N08 itself from the west.
    road_heads: [
        (name: ("Western track", "Західна дорога"), at: (-470.0, -1785.0)),
        (name: ("Eastern track", "Східна дорога"), at: (704.0, -1785.0)),
        (name: ("N08, west", "Н08, захід"), at: (-2350.0, -1700.0)),
    ],

    // The Russian guns have every lane registered: where the tracks cross the minefields.
    trps: [
        OnLine("west", (-497.0, -340.0)), OnLine("west", (-492.0, 160.0)), OnLine("west", (-488.0, 420.0)),
        OnLine("east", (666.0, -340.0)), OnLine("east", (661.0, 160.0)), OnLine("east", (657.0, 420.0)),
    ],

    // Last year's wrecks, from the Russian advance in 2022, still in the fields.
    old_wrecks: [(At((-1180.0, -180.0)), 2.4), (At((1480.0, 330.0)), 0.9), (At((150.0, -620.0)), 4.1)],

    advance: 1.0,
    foothold_z: 662.0,
    defence_z: 702.0,
    // The 291st's trench along the northern edge of the crest belt, and the 47th's start line in the forward tree
    // line, where its ATGM teams overwatch the attack.
    trench_z: Some(702.0),
    // A year of shelling between the lines: 240 craters, from the forward minefield to the crest.
    shelled: Some((240, -480.0, 1250.0)),
    start_z: Some(-900.0),
    home: (-200.0, -1600.0),
    jam_z: 100.0,
    mortar_band: (-600.0, 702.0),

    // ---- The battle's part (bav_sim::data) ----

    // The 47th's side as Units and Support (design/command.md): what the brigade had for the breach, with the 33rd's
    // Leopard 2A6s, and what it cost in allotment points. June 2023: at most about 55 guns on the whole axis (RUSI),
    // so a battery's morning for the breach; the Russian guns had 35 days of ammunition at the gun line.
    catalog: [
        (id: "stugna", name: ("Stugna-P team", "Розрахунок «Стугни-П»"), what: Post(Some(Stugna)), cost: 8, supply: 5, available: 4),
        (id: "javelin", name: ("Javelin team", "Розрахунок «Джавеліна»"), what: Post(Some(Javelin)), cost: 9, supply: 5, available: 3),
        (id: "rifles", name: ("Rifle section", "Стрілецьке відділення"), what: Post(None), cost: 3, supply: 2, available: 5),
        (id: "leo2r", name: ("Leopard 2R mine plow", "Leopard 2R з тралом"), what: Vehicle(Leo2r), cost: 12, supply: 8, available: 3),
        (id: "bmr2", name: ("BMR-2 mine clearer", "БМР-2"), what: Vehicle(Bmr2), cost: 8, supply: 5, available: 2),
        (id: "wisent", name: ("Wisent 1 engineer tank", "Wisent 1"), what: Vehicle(Wisent), cost: 10, supply: 6, available: 1),
        (id: "leo2a6", name: ("Leopard 2A6", "Leopard 2A6"), what: Vehicle(Leo2a6), cost: 12, supply: 8, available: 4),
        (id: "bradley", name: ("M2A2 Bradley, with its squad", "M2A2 Bradley з десантом"), what: Vehicle(Bradley), cost: 6, supply: 4, available: 20),
        (id: "evac", name: ("Bradley for the wounded", "Бредлі на евакуацію"), what: Evacuation, cost: 5, supply: 4, available: 6),
    ],
    support: [
        (id: "155", name: ("155 mm, 16 rounds", "155 мм, 16 пострілів"), what: Shells(16), cost: 4, available: 8),
        (id: "himars", name: ("HIMARS mission", "Удар HIMARS"), what: Himars, cost: 8, available: 2),
        (id: "smoke", name: ("Smoke mission", "Димова завіса"), what: Smoke, cost: 1, available: 10),
        (id: "brigade", name: ("Brigade guns, 20 rounds", "Бригадна артилерія, 20 пострілів"), what: Brigade(20), cost: 2, available: 40),
        (id: "mortar", name: ("120 mm mortars, 20 bombs", "Міномети 120 мм, 20 мін"), what: Mortar(20), cost: 1, available: 8),
        // FPVs were still scarce on this front in June 2023 (db/research/10 §3); a few minutes in the air.
        (id: "fpv", name: ("FPV strike drone", "FPV-дрон"), what: Fpv, cost: 3, available: 3),
        // Command only, not the day's: a battery behind the start line with a few missiles, which gets a shot at a Ka-52
        // when it pops up to fire; and more reconnaissance drones for the operator.
        (id: "ad", name: ("Air defence on call, 3 missiles", "ППО на виклик, 3 ракети"), what: AirDefence(3), cost: 10, available: 2),
        (id: "mavic", name: ("Two more Mavic 3s", "Ще два Mavic 3"), what: Mavic(2), cost: 3, available: 2),
    ],
    // The Record: the overwatch in the forward tree line; the breach's twenty vehicles (the script's two groups);
    // four Bradleys held back at the start line for the wounded; 64 rounds, one HIMARS and six smoke missions for the
    // player's battery, the brigade's guns, the mortars, and one strike drone. 304 of 310 points.
    allotment: (
        points: 310,
        // Command's Supply: what there is at the start, and what comes up each minute of the day's clock.
        supply: (16, 2.0),
        record: [
            (id: "stugna", at: Some(0)), (id: "stugna", at: Some(1)), (id: "javelin", at: Some(2)), (id: "rifles", at: Some(3)),
            (id: "rifles", at: Some(4)),
            (id: "leo2r", count: 2), (id: "bmr2"), (id: "wisent"), (id: "leo2a6", count: 3), (id: "bradley", count: 13),
            (id: "evac", count: 4),
            (id: "155", count: 4), (id: "himars"), (id: "smoke", count: 6), (id: "brigade", count: 30), (id: "mortar", count: 4), (id: "fpv"),
        ],
    ),
    // The 291st's Kornets on the crest, covering both tracks.
    ru_weapons: [None, Some(Kornet), Some(Kornet), None, Some(Kornet), None, None],
    // The 291st's T-72B3s, dug in hull-down on the crest behind the trench, facing north.
    dug_in: [((-150.0, 724.0), 0.15), ((1050.0, 720.0), -0.1)],
    old_wreck_kinds: [T72, Bmp2, Mtlb, T72, Bmp2, Mtlb, T72, Bmp2],
    // Space orders the ATGM teams or our column; Shift+click calls RAAM or smoke; the enemy's guns and their habits.
    space_key: Column,
    shift_fire: Smoke,
    ru_guns: Some(Column(seen_z: -650.0, field: (-1800.0, 1800.0, -1500.0, -850.0))),
    registered_fire: (90.0, 4),
    // The drone team behind the start line; south of Mala Tokmachka it is hard to find.
    // Command's Enemy staff (bav_sim::staff): the Lancets hunted the Leopards here (c09 §5); the Orlans watch the slope.
    staff: (lancets: 4, orlan: (120.0, 240.0)),
    operator: (pos: (-300.0, -960.0), found_per_hour: 0.05),
    // Their EW (db/research/11 §5): platoon jammers in the second line behind the crest, each switched on and off, the heavier emitters
    // further back felt past the jam line; and GNSS jamming lifted about a minute before each Ka-52 run.
    ew: Some((jammers: [(-1100.0, 950.0), (-350.0, 950.0), (400.0, 950.0), (1150.0, 950.0)], radius: 1100.0, depth: 700.0, ka52_tell: true)),
    // A strike drone flies a few minutes.
    fpv: Some((endurance: 300.0)),
    // The Bradleys held back at the start line for the wounded, sent one at a time where the player asks.
    evacuation: Some((kind: Bradley, start: 900.0)),

    // Mala Tokmachka, 8 June 2023 (c09 §2, §6 set piece 1, §11 on the date): the guns finish their preparation in
    // the dark; the column is late and moves off at first light; nine vehicles behind a Leopard 2R and a BMR-2 on the
    // western track, eleven on the eastern; Ka-52s from beyond reach; four Bradleys back in for the men; and in the
    // end, everyone back to the start line. 03:50 to late morning in about 25 minutes. That morning four Bradleys
    // went back in for the men; here they go when the player sends them (`evacuation`), not on the clock.
    script: [
        (1.0, Say("Bird up. Still dark. Our guns are working the crest.")),
        (3.0, Prep(missions: 14, over: 70.0)),
        (8.0, Say("All, this is {command}. The column is late. The guns will be finished before it gets there.")),
        (85.0, Say("This is {op}. Guns are done. Nothing on the track yet.")),
        (110.0, Column(route: 0, kinds: [Leo2r, Bmr2, Leo2a6, Bradley, Bradley, Bradley, Bradley, Bradley, Bradley], plow: true, smoke: 0, start: 350.0, label: "04:23  The first group moves off behind the plows. It is getting light.")),
        (125.0, Say("This is {op}. First group on the western track. Nine vehicles. The Leopard with the plow in front, the rollers behind it.")),
        (150.0, Jam(0.4)),
        (330.0, Column(route: 1, kinds: [Leo2r, Wisent, Leo2a6, Bradley, Bradley, Bradley, Bradley, Leo2a6, Bradley, Bradley, Bradley], plow: true, smoke: 0, start: 280.0, label: "05:29  The second group, eleven vehicles, on the eastern track")),
        (345.0, Say("This is {op}. Second group moving. Same plan, the other track.")),
        (430.0, Helicopters([(2900.0, 3000.0), (3500.0, 2650.0)])),
        (436.0, Say("Ka-52s! Two of them, south-east, low over the ridge. Too far for anything we have.")),
        (770.0, Helicopters([(-3100.0, 2900.0), (-2500.0, 3300.0)])),
        (776.0, Say("This is {op}. Helicopters again. South-west this time.")),
        (1000.0, Order(PullBack)),
        (1300.0, Say("This is {op}. Quiet on the lanes. Only the smoke.")),
    ],
)
